From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: no LOFT LUT base on 2.4 GHz

The LO leakage LUTs get a per-core base that follows the 5 GHz pa5g
sub-band group. On 2.4 GHz the group was derived from a 5 GHz frequency
made up from the channel number, which put the group 0 base on core 2.
wl 7.14 has no base on 2.4 GHz: all three LUTs are zero on channels 1, 6
and 11.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c
@@ -7631,7 +7631,8 @@ static u16 b43_phy_ac_loft_add(u16 a, u1
  *   3           0           f6fb, ec00 from 0x1b      fafb, f6f6 from 0x1d
  *
  * Why the base exists, why the step falls where it does and why it follows
- * the pa5g partition is not known; only that it does.
+ * the pa5g partition is not known; only that it does. On 2.4 GHz there is
+ * none: wl 7.14 leaves all three LUTs at zero on channels 1, 6 and 11.
  */
 static u16 b43_phy_ac_loft_lut_base(struct b43_wldev *dev, unsigned int core,
 				    unsigned int off)
@@ -7639,7 +7640,7 @@ static u16 b43_phy_ac_loft_lut_base(stru
 	unsigned int grp = b43_phy_ac_pa5g_group(dev,
 			5000 + 5 * dev->phy.ac->cal_channel);
 
-	if (core == 0)
+	if (core == 0 || b43_current_band(dev->wl) == NL80211_BAND_2GHZ)
 		return 0x0000;
 	if (core == 1) {
 		if (grp < 3)
